  title "Light and Ruin"
  summary "Light-Regent Xouhoulong of Aurora Stack designs an elaborate plaza to maintain the fragile Accord between the Aurora Stack and Nightshelf colonies, but his reliance on hidden diplomacy and the doctrine of Mandatum∴absconditu (two truths, two economies) leads him to secretly authorize research into Wake-Singer magic and negotiate a pact with orca clans. When the research chambers awaken something ancient in the ice and a catastrophic Calving kills High-Beak Auditor Selka, the sealed galleries become corruption corridors that undermine the very plaza Xouhoulong built. Grand Auditor Qeihong's investigation exposes the deception, and Xouhoulong is displaced from power, left standing before the darkness his own architecture created—a monument to how the gap between what is said and what is done, when hidden long enough, becomes a chasm that destroys everything it was meant to protect."
